    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d546">

                <pb facs="1378" n="1362" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/3–751: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the United States Delegation to
                        the Torquay Conference</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Corse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Torquay</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-03-07T17:00:00+00:00">March 7, 1951—5 p.
                            m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>518. At final session multilateral negots group, memo adopted along lines
                    reported previous tel.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d546-f1"/> All countries stated
                    intent sign immediately except following: UK dissented. France and Italy stated
                    awaiting signing authority. Can maintained observer role.</p>
                <p>Rpt to London 218, Paris for OSR 56, and Rome
                    18.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corse</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d546-f1" n="1" xml:id="d546-f1-content">
                <p>Apparently the reference is to Torquay telegram 497, March 3, <ref
                        target="#pg1359">p. 1359</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
